  "description": "WUTNOQ crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P 1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C112 H132 Eu2 N12 O28 Tb4. From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 4 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 4 O neighbors; Tb1 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.786-3.878 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 86.03-105.16°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula Eu2Tb4C112H132N12O28. Article name explicitly identifies Eu(II), Tb(III).",
